  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is the ratio of energies of photons produced due to transition of an electron of hydrogen atom from its</p><p>(i) third permitted energy level to the second level and</p><p>(ii) the highest permitted energy level to the second permitted level.</p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Energy of a photon released in transition of electron in hydrogen atom is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8734;</mo></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
